  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22179268
    description: >-
      Zenodo concept DOI. Always resolves to the latest
      archived version.
abstract: >-
  A first-principles model of a counterflow wet cooling tower,
  coupled to an ion-association water-chemistry engine, that
  evaluates each scale-forming mineral at the temperature where
  it is least soluble: calcite, calcium phosphates, brucite and
  gypsum at the hot condenser tube skin, amorphous silica at the
  cold tower basin. Acceptance criteria were fixed before each
  calculation. The tower criteria were scored on a campaign-wise
  holdout of published pilot-tower data and re-scored, with
  thresholds unchanged, after
  duplicated rows were found in the published data and again after
  the pilot tower was solved at its site pressure. The failures are
  reported as failures and no threshold was moved. Includes a
  PHREEQC 3.9.0 benchmark grid, an independent MATLAB and Simulink
  re-implementation (verified against the Python core to 1.4e-5 K
  at the sea-level calibration), the pre-registration records, and
  a register of the defects found in the author's own work, each
  with the result it moved.
keywords:
  - cooling tower
  - district cooling
  - condenser water
  - water treatment
  - scale prediction
  - thermodynamics
  - process control
  - reproducible research
